# Paths a build excludes from the card-platform root context.
#
# This file governs a build that names no ignore file of its own. Each
# services/*/Dockerfile has one — services/<service>/Dockerfile.dockerignore — and BuildKit
# reads that one instead of this one, so the six service images are not governed here. What
# remains for this file is an ad-hoc build run against this directory, and it excludes the
# same things for the same reasons.

# Host build output. Every image builds from source in its own builder stage, so an archive
# built on the host has no part in any image and must not reach one.
**/target/

# Local environment values. .env.example travels with the repository; the .env a
# developer copies from it carries their own credentials, as does .demo-credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.demo-credentials

# Documentation, the executive presentation and the Kubernetes manifests. No
# stage of any image build reads them.
docs/
presentation/
deploy/

# A Maven repository checked into a context belongs in no image. A builder stage resolves
# through a BuildKit cache mount, which is not part of the context at all.
.m2/

# Editor and operating-system artifacts.
**/*.swp
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
